<title>UK: Scott Pickford says court orders share swap.</title>
<headline>Scott Pickford says court orders share swap.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British oil services company Scott Pickford Plc said a British court ruled on Tuesday that the proposed share exchange with Australia's Aerodata Holdings Ltd take place within the next seven days.</p>
<p>Aerodata is fighting U.S.-based laboratory services group Core Laboratories NV for control of Scott Pickford. The share exchange has become key to the takeover fight.</p>
<p>Scott Pickford said its application for an appeal against the ruling was refused.</p>
<p>On Monday Core raised its bid for Scott Pickford, offering 59p per share on condition that Scott Pickford abandoned the proposed share exchange with Aerodata. The increased offer values Scott Pickford at around 7.5 million stg, Core said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
